    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d320">

                <pb facs="0468" n="456" xml:id="pg456"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.6131/595: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Thurston</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1940-08-06T21:00:00+03:00">August 6, 1940—9
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received August 6—3 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>976. Exchange of notes extending commercial agreement to August 6, 1941,
                    including notes on Soviet coal, took place at 8 o’clock Moscow time tonight.
                    Details follow in a separate telegram.<anchor n="71" xml:id="d320-f1"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Thurston</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>[For text of the agreement effected by exchange of notes signed August 6,
                        1940, and effective August 6, 1940, see Department of State Executive
                        Agreement Series No. 179, or 54 Stat. (pt. 2) 2366. For text of press
                        release issued by the Department August 7, see Department of State <hi
                            rendition="#italic">Bulletin</hi>, August 10, 1940, page 105.]</p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d320-f1" n="71" xml:id="d320-f1-content">
                <p>Telegram No. 982, August 7, 11 a.m., from the Chargé in the Soviet Union, <ref
